### Phase 3.2 — CBT Exam Engine (complete)

Backend (`backend/cbt/` extended):
- `CBTExam` model: school FK, title, subject FK, class_arms M2M (ClassArm), term FK, session FK (AcademicSession), created_by FK, start_datetime, end_datetime, duration_minutes, instructions, selection_mode (manual/random_from_bank), manual_questions M2M (Question), random_config (JSONField: [{topic_id, count, difficulty?}]), randomize_questions, randomize_options, allow_review, show_score_immediately, status (draft/published/ongoing/completed)
  - `resolve_questions()`: handles both manual and random pool drawing + shuffle
- `StudentExamSession` model: exam FK, student FK, question_order (JSONField: list of question IDs), option_maps (JSONField: {str(q_id): {original_option_id: shuffled_option_id}}), started_at, submitted_at, time_remaining_seconds, status (not_started/in_progress/submitted/timed_out), score (Decimal %), tab_switch_count, ip_address — unique_together (exam, student)
- `StudentAnswer` model: exam_session FK, question FK, selected_option, is_correct (null until submit), time_spent_seconds — unique_together (exam_session, question)

Endpoints added to `/api/cbt/exams/`:
- `GET available/` — exams for logged-in student's class arm, annotated with session_status + score
- `POST {id}/start/` — creates/resumes session; shuffles questions and options; returns questions WITHOUT correct_answer or explanation; marks exam `ongoing`
- `POST {id}/save-answer/` — body: {question_id, selected_option, time_spent_seconds}; upserts StudentAnswer
- `GET {id}/status/` — recalculates time_remaining from started_at; returns session status + all saved answers
- `POST {id}/submit/` — marks every answer correct/incorrect (reverses option shuffle map before comparing); computes percentage score; returns score + optionally full answer breakdown if show_score_immediately
- `POST {id}/log-tab-switch/` — increments tab_switch_count

Key logic:
- Option shuffle stored per question as `{original_id: shuffled_id}`; submit reverses map to get original before comparing to `Question.correct_answer`
- Fill-blank graded with `.strip().lower()` compare
- Timer: time_remaining computed live as `duration_minutes * 60 - elapsed_since_started_at`

